  "notes": "Official Ila Faye Miller School of Nursing and Health Professions Traditional BSN degree plan (published 02/2025; approved by the Texas Board of Nursing; 28-month, five-semester nursing sequence after prerequisites). Minimum 122 hours for graduation. Two courses are conditional and modeled as 0-credit choice slots excluded from the 122 total: (a) NURS 2199 Seminar for Health Professions (1 credit) is recommended but NOT required, so freshman Fall is 17 hours (18 with it); (b) the second CHEM 1320 row in freshman Spring (3 credits) applies only if chemistry placement dictates, so freshman Spring is 13 hours (16 with it): 17+13+17+16+16+16+15+12 = 122, matching the document's stated total. Freshman Fall chemistry is a 3-credit slot: CHEM 1310 OR CHEM 1320, based on UIW chemistry placement. RELS/PHIL upper-level ethics slot applies only if the student did not take RELS 1330. No per-course prerequisites given in the plan; prereq arrays left empty, see source.",
